WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:03.166
What happens when 800 of the world’s most elite footballers...

00:00:03.166 --> 00:00:06.125
and their managers live together under one roof?

00:00:06.166 --> 00:00:07.875
Players stop being polite...

00:00:07.875 --> 00:00:09.791
and start getting Re-al.

00:00:09.791 --> 00:00:10.666
This is…

00:00:10.666 --> 00:00:11.958
The Champions.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.375
Some say I’m the best in the world…

00:00:14.916 --> 00:00:16.791
I agree with them.

00:00:16.833 --> 00:00:17.958
I’m Lionel Messi.

00:00:17.958 --> 00:00:19.791
I let my football speak for itself…

00:00:20.083 --> 00:00:22.875
I should have played for the Spanish team.

00:00:23.541 --> 00:00:24.708
Say your name!

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.083
Kevin.

00:00:26.541 --> 00:00:28.916
People said I couldn’t carry Egypt...

00:00:28.916 --> 00:00:30.416
They were right.

00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:45.583
So today is arrival day,

00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:48.750
and I’m going to be meeting my new Juventus teammates.

00:00:48.791 --> 00:00:50.583
It’s hard because in Italy...

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:53.000
they are very focused on image.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.750
It’s, like, all about their looks,

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:55.416
their hair,

00:00:55.416 --> 00:00:56.250
their tan.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.000
It’s all very new to me.

00:00:58.041 --> 00:01:00.916
I’m trying to connect to the average Italian,

00:01:00.916 --> 00:01:03.625
so I bought the typical Italian car,

00:01:03.625 --> 00:01:06.375
some traditional Italian clothing,

00:01:06.375 --> 00:01:08.791
and I’ve been reading up on local politics.

00:01:25.541 --> 00:01:27.791
Leo, what’s good, my man!

00:01:29.791 --> 00:01:31.333
Happiest day of my life?

00:01:32.041 --> 00:01:33.875
When my son was born,

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.500
winning my 5th Ballon d’Or, um...

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:40.750
Neymar leaving Barcelona.

00:01:45.625 --> 00:01:47.125
OK, so I like the colors,

00:01:47.125 --> 00:01:49.375
but I would make, uh, one quick change.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:50.708
Hey, what are you doing?

00:01:50.708 --> 00:01:52.750
I’m improving la decoracion!

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.000
That’s not an improvement

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.791
Of course it is. We got further in the World Cup--

00:01:55.791 --> 00:01:57.333
Hey! You guys,

00:01:57.333 --> 00:02:00.000
this isn’t about what country we’re from.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.708
This about PSG, man.

00:02:01.708 --> 00:02:03.416
This is about Paris.

00:02:03.416 --> 00:02:04.166
This is about...

00:02:04.166 --> 00:02:05.833
France, baby. Yeah!

00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:08.500
Oh wow! Look, everybody, Mbappe brought the World Cup.

00:02:08.541 --> 00:02:10.583
Oh he’s such a prodigy, so good, so young.

00:02:10.625 --> 00:02:12.041
And he donates all his money to charity.

00:02:12.041 --> 00:02:12.791
Mbappe?

00:02:12.791 --> 00:02:13.666
I mean yeah,

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:14.750
so he won a World Cup.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:15.666
He’s good.

00:02:16.541 --> 00:02:18.083
Still hasn’t won a Puskas.

00:02:25.791 --> 00:02:27.958
Still a little wide of the woodwork, eh, bruv?

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.125
Man’s got jokes, eh?

00:02:29.125 --> 00:02:31.250
I do have jokes. In fact, I've got...

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.708
I noticed some of me English mates were bickering...

00:02:33.708 --> 00:02:36.083
so I thought I’d take some of the Three Lions...

00:02:36.083 --> 00:02:37.166
to go explore the gardens.

00:02:37.166 --> 00:02:38.958
A little English bonding time, ya know?

00:02:39.416 --> 00:02:40.333
Come along, lads!

00:02:40.333 --> 00:02:41.625
I’ll lead the way!

00:02:46.791 --> 00:02:48.541
I thought you said you could take us home.

00:02:48.541 --> 00:02:49.416
I know, I can.

00:02:49.416 --> 00:02:50.875
I can. It’s right there.

00:02:50.875 --> 00:02:52.333
We just need to get over that, uh,

00:02:52.333 --> 00:02:52.875
semifinal.

00:02:52.875 --> 00:02:54.041
I mean, uh, that hill.

00:02:54.041 --> 00:02:55.500
Don’t worry...I’ve got this.

00:02:56.375 --> 00:02:58.541
I thought you said you could take us home, Harry.

00:02:58.541 --> 00:03:00.333
Oh, me leg is having a cramp.

00:03:00.333 --> 00:03:01.750
I’m having a cramp, Harry.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:02.416
Take me home!

00:03:02.416 --> 00:03:03.125
I’m scared, Harry!

00:03:03.125 --> 00:03:04.500
I want to go home.

00:03:05.208 --> 00:03:06.166
I tried!

00:03:06.166 --> 00:03:07.791
I didn’t ask for all this pressure.

00:03:07.791 --> 00:03:10.125
But I swear on the grave of King Richard,

00:03:10.125 --> 00:03:11.375
I gave it me all...

00:03:11.375 --> 00:03:13.375
and I’d trade in all me golden boots...

00:03:13.375 --> 00:03:15.083
and me feets and all me toes...

00:03:15.083 --> 00:03:18.333
for one more chance of making the bloody final.

00:03:18.333 --> 00:03:20.041
Aw, Harry,

00:03:20.041 --> 00:03:21.375
I’m so sorry, mate.

00:03:21.375 --> 00:03:22.375
It’s just,

00:03:22.375 --> 00:03:25.000
none of us have any idea what you just said.

